fastapi.hooks:
### Ruff Linting Hook
Automatically fixes lint issues when Python files are saved.

This repo uses ruff for linting (configured in `pyproject.toml` with a `[tool.ruff]` section). Running it automatically prevents lint failures from accumulating and keeps code style consistent across the large FastAPI codebase.

Add to `.claude/settings.json`:
```json
{
  "hooks": {
    "postToolExecution": [
      {
        "matcher": "Write|Edit",
        "globs": ["fastapi/**/*.py", "tests/**/*.py"],
        "command": "ruff check --fix \"$FILE_PATH\"",
        "description": "Auto-fix lint issues with ruff"
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

**Setup**: Ruff is already in the `docs-tests` dependency group. Install with `uv sync --group tests`.

---

### MyPy Type Checking Hook
Validates type annotations when Python files are modified.

This repo enforces strict typing with mypy (in the `tests` dependency group) and requires 100% type coverage. Running mypy on save catches type errors early and prevents regressions in the type-safe API surface that FastAPI exposes.

Add to `.claude/settings.json`:
```json
{
  "hooks": {
    "postToolExecution": [
      {
        "matcher": "Write|Edit",
        "globs": ["fastapi/**/*.py"],
        "command": "mypy \"$FILE_PATH\" --no-error-summary 2>&1 | head -20",
        "description": "Type-check with mypy",
        "continueOnError": true
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

**Setup**: MyPy is in the `tests` dependency group. Install with `uv sync --group tests`. The hook limits output to 20 lines to avoid noise; full checking happens in CI.

